        "narrative": "<p>Fair numbers of lake trout were present, with fish as large as 24 inches taken.  Half the lake trout collected had been produced naturally; the rest had been stocked as yearlings in 1987.  Lake trout growth had been about average for a Cook County lake trout lake.  Smallmouth bass were fairly abundant, with good growth.  Rainbow smelt were still present in the lake, but probably not in sufficient numbers to be an important source of forage for lake trout.  Northern cisco were abundant, and provided forage for large lake trout, but may have competed with small lake trout for invertebrate forage.  No other gamefish were collected, which has been typical of Duncan Lake.</p>",
