        "narrative": "<p>Lake trout were abundant but small, and were mostly survivors from 1988 and 1987 yearling stockings.  Lake trout natural reproduction seemed to be limited.  A few smallmouth bass were collected, and their abundance appeared to be within the normal range for lakes of this type.  Smallmouth bass growth was slow, and no fish over 15 inches were collected.  No other gamefish species were collected; however, walleye and northern pike may be present in low numbers - both species were found in the lake in the 1970's.</p>",
